{
    "background_story": "Frances was a brilliant inventor with a passion for making life easier for others. Growing up, she watched her mother struggle with meal prep, juggling multiple pots and pans on the stovetop. This sparked an idea in Frances, and she set out to create a device that could quickly and safely cook food. After years of experimentation, she successfully developed the first domestic microwave oven. Her invention revolutionized the way people cooked, freeing up time for more important things. Frances's microwave quickly became a staple in kitchens around the world, and she continued to innovate, improving her design and making it more accessible to all. Her legacy as a pioneer in kitchen technology remains, and her name is synonymous with convenience and innovation.",
